// Groups for "Clusters" and "Odd One Out". A Clusters puzzle takes one group
// from each level and four words from each, so every group has more words than
// a puzzle needs. An Odd One Out set takes three words from one group and one
// from another group of the same kind.
//
// Each group:
//   id      unique, stable (progress is stored against it)
//   level   1 (straightforward) to 4 (tricky); a puzzle has one of each
//   kind    what its words are: people, places, things, words, books, or
//           story (words from one story, of any sort)
//   title   what the four words share, shown once the group is found
//   note    a sentence or two explaining the link
//   items   [word, reference] or [word, reference, find]: a word that can go in
//           a puzzle, with a passage that shows it belongs. `find` is a phrase in
//           that passage, checked by scripts/check-data.mjs; it defaults to the
//           word itself. Book groups (`books: true`) give each book's first verse.
//   fits    optional: other words that would also belong. A puzzle never shows a
//           word that belongs to two of its groups, whether it is listed in
//           `items` or `fits`, so every answer has exactly one right group.
//   family  optional: groups that share a family are never in the same puzzle
//           (their stories overlap too much to keep apart)
//
// Scripture references and spellings follow the World English Bible.
